    "created_at": "2016-11-30T07:46:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-11-30T07:50:31Z",
    "body": "My understanding is that this is working as intended: it allows you to do `location.protocol = \"https\"` and the browser treats it as if you had provided `location.protocol = \"https:\"`. This is how all browsers work today from what I understand. It also treats `location.protocol = \"https:\"` as if you had provided `location.protocol = \"https::\"` (i.e. `\"https:\"` followed by `\":\"`), but I believe the \"basic URL parse\" algorithm will just ignore the extra colon.\r\n\r\n@annevk?",
